    The priority queue will use this to order states.
    Lower priority = explored first.


    def heuristic(self):
        return sum(
            abs(i//3 - self.goal.index(tile)//3) + abs(i%3 - self.goal.index(tile)%3)
            for i, tile in enumerate(self.board) if tile != 0
        )

This calculates the Manhattan Distance heuristic.

Breaking it down:

  enumerate(self.board) produces (index, value) pairs:
    (0, 1), (1, 2), (2, 5), (3, 3), (4, 4), (5, 0), (6, 6), (7, 7), (8, 8)

  For each (i, tile) pair where tile != 0 (skip the blank):

    i = current flat list index of this tile in the CURRENT board
    tile = the tile's number/value

    self.goal.index(tile) = flat list index of this tile in the GOAL board

    Convert current position to 2D:
      current_row = i // 3
      current_col = i % 3

    Convert goal position to 2D:
      goal_row = self.goal.index(tile) // 3
      goal_col = self.goal.index(tile) % 3

    Manhattan distance for this one tile:
      abs(current_row - goal_row) + abs(current_col - goal_col)

    abs() = absolute value (makes negative numbers positive)

  sum(...) adds up all individual tile Manhattan distances.


    def neighbors(self):
        n = []
        r, c = divmod(self.blank, 3)
        for dr, dc in ((-1,0),(1,0),(0,-1),(0,1)):
            nr, nc = r+dr, c+dc
            if 0 <= nr < 3 and 0 <= nc < 3:
                nb = self.board[:]
                j = nr*3 + nc
                nb[self.blank], nb[j] = nb[j], nb[self.blank]
                n.append(PuzzleState(nb, self.goal, self.moves+1, self))
